Intended use
------------

This map is intended to use with water O (smiles notation). It can be applied both for H2O and HOD, but gives the frequency of the OH stretch.

The goal here is to select the correct coupling map. For intramolecular couplings a special map must be used as the dipole dipole map is not reliable.

How to use
----------
This is not a stand-alone map. It must however be requested when running water couplings to properly distribute between intramolecular and intermolecular couplings.


Available parameters
--------------------
When using this map, the following parameters become available in any input parameter source file (default file, input file, command line):

Water.coupling_choice
    no shorthand
    options: None, DipDip, Water_Intra

If one wants to do bulk water (H2O) the Water_Intra or DipDip can both be used, however, for all intramolecular couplings Water_Intra will always be used and for intermolecular couplings DipDip will always be used.
If one wants to do isotope labeled water (HOD) the couplings should not be calculated and None must be selected.

Warnings that can be raised by this map
